# vzhn/kater-fork#27: three method calls that lin orders in a circle; psc
# relates the SC write e8 to itself (e8 po e9 hb e7 po e8). The full
# isConsistent of IMM used to accept the graph, as its search from the SC
# write e5 finished the pairs of the hb loop first and never went back to
# them; with T1 and T2 swapped it rejected it.
e0: T0 METHOD-BEGIN na
e1: T0 METHOD-END na
e2: T1 TB acq
e3: T1 METHOD-BEGIN na
e4: T1 METHOD-END na
e5: T1 W(x) sc
e6: T2 TB acq
e7: T2 METHOD-BEGIN na
e8: T2 W(y) sc
e9: T2 METHOD-END na
mo(x): e5
mo(y): e8
lin: e1->e3 e4->e7 e9->e0
